* **Mixed-event method**: Suppose the particle distributions are similar in events with similar collision environment. So the uncorrelated background can be reconstructed by pairing particles in current event with those in other similar events, as is demonstrated in Fig. 4.5. In this analysis, the events are classified according to the collision centrality and the position of primary vertex along the beam-line.

